    {
     "source": "s11",
     "quote": "Holometaboly, or complete metamorphosis, refers to insects such as beetles, flies, butterflies, moths and bees, which hatch as wormlike larvae that eventually enter a quiescent pupal stage",
     "quoteLang": "en",
     "verbatim": true
